<title>NETHERLANDS: Lanschot sees Beter Bed outperforming.</title>
<headline>Lanschot sees Beter Bed outperforming.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of March 12 research.</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>Beter Bed	 Retail	  32.90   Van Lanschot</p>
<p>COMMENT: OUTPERFORMANCE. Stock will outperform the market in six to twelve months. Beter Bed announced 1996 net profit of 11.2 million guilders and EPS rose 27.7 pct to 1.86 guilders. In 1997 EPS could grow by 23.7 pct. The chain grew by six shops in 1996 and for 1997 at least six shops are planned. Together with a wholesaler in baby products, Beter Bed is starting a baby chain: Beter Baby. Fast improvement is expected in gross margin of Dormael, which they recently acquired.</p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):  EPS	P/E    P/CF   Dividend</p>
<p>    1996 (actual)     1.86     17.7   12.7   0.65</p>
<p>    1997		  2.30     14.3   10.6   0.81</p>
<p>    1998		  2.72     12.1    9.4   0.96</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
